---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";

const title = `Privacy Policy | ${profile.name}`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description="Privacy policy for mariusbleif.com.">
  <a href="/" class="inline-block mb-8 opacity-60 transition hover:opacity-100">&larr; mariusbleif.com</a>
  <article class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-2xl prose-headings:font-normal prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:underline-offset-4">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      This policy explains how personal data is processed when you visit
      mariusbleif.com. It follows the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP)
      and, where it applies, the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Marius Bleif<br />
      c/o JL Consulting Group GmbH#1652<br />
      Zürcherstrasse 84<br />
      8852 Altendorf<br />
      Schweiz<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. The website</h2>
    <p>
      mariusbleif.com is a static website. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics,
      has no forms or accounts and loads no third-party scripts or fonts;
      everything the page needs is served from the site itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only data processed is the standard technical data the hosting provider
      records whenever a page is requested: IP address, date and time, the page
      requested, browser and operating system, and the referring page. These
      server logs are used to deliver the site and keep it secure, and are deleted
      after a short period.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Netlify, Inc., 512 2nd Street, Suite 200, San
      Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Netlify is certified under the Swiss-U.S. Data
      Privacy Framework. See
      <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Netlify's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      The site contains links to other websites. No data is passed to them until
      you follow a link; from then on their own privacy policies apply.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to me, I process the data you send in order to answer you. It
      is kept for as long as the correspondence requires and then deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Purposes and legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Data is processed only to deliver the site, keep it secure and answer your
      requests. Under the FADP no separate legal basis is required for such
      proportionate processing. Where the GDPR applies, the basis is my
      legitimate interest in running a secure website and in responding to
      correspondence (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>6. Transfer abroad</h2>
    <p>
      The hosting provider is based in the USA. The transfer relies on its
      certification under the Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, which the Swiss
      Federal Council recognises as providing adequate protection.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You may ask, free of charge, for access to the personal data held about
      you, and for its correction or deletion. Write to
      <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>; I may need to
      verify your identity first. You may also lodge a complaint with the Federal
      Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC), Feldeggweg 1, 3003
      Bern, Switzerland, or, where the GDPR applies, with the supervisory
      authority responsible for you.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be revised when the site or the law changes. The version
      published here applies.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
